------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB-SOURCE PARITY (every branch reproduced natively)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Web ScoreBadge is a letter-grade pill (A+ / A / B / C / D / F / —) where the letter IS the badge — no
"SCORE" sub-label. It takes EITHER a numeric `score` (mapped via `numericToGrade`, optionally with
custom `thresholds`) OR a pre-computed `grade`, plus a `size`; the colour comes from the shared grade
palette so any badge with the same letter renders the same colour. Reproduced verbatim:
  * numericToGrade(score, thresholds): null/!finite -> '—' (unrated); else thresholds evaluated
    highest-first, first `score >= min` wins; below all -> 'F'. Ported as ScoreBadgeScale.grade(for:).
  * DEFAULT_SCORE_THRESHOLDS: A+ >= 90, A >= 80, B >= 65, C >= 50, D >= 35, F >= 0 (lower bound
    inclusive) — ported as ScoreBadgeScale.defaultThresholds.
  * GRADE_PALETTE -> P1/S9 semantic tokens (no raw hex): A+/A -> success (#10b981), B -> info
    (#00f0ff), C -> warning (#f59e0b), D/F -> danger (the #ef4444 / #b91c1c shade distinction
    collapses to the single semantic danger token; the glyph differentiates the two), '—' -> muted
    text (#6b7280).
  * SIZE_CLASS: sm = text-xs (12pt), md = text-xl (20pt), lg = text-3xl (30pt); bold, tabular figures
    (`.monospacedDigit()`), tight leading — the web `font-bold leading-none tabular-nums`.
  * aria-label: `ariaLabel ?? t('score.aria', 'Score {{grade}}', { grade: info.label })` — ported as
    ScoreBadgeAriaBuilder (the i18next `{{grade}}` becomes a width-/locale-safe `%@`). The override
    (web `ariaLabel`) wins when present. Web `className` / `testId` are DOM-only — no native peer.
States rendered (no hidden surface): loading skeleton · unavailable retry chip · ready(A+/A/B/C/D/F)
· empty (the '—' unrated glyph IS the resolved-but-null-score empty readout, never a blank box) ·
stale (warning marker + one-shot auto-refresh) · offline (cached glyph + offline marker). P4 leaf
contract layered on the prop-driven web badge: crossing INTO the `stale` band arms a single
auto-refresh; offline never auto-refreshes. Telemetry view.opened emitted once on first ready (slug
"ScoreBadge"). All copy via the P1/S10 i18n facade; all colour via P1/S9 tokens; TSButton / TSSkeleton
reused; no Tailwind ports, no raw hex. All public types prefixed `ScoreBadge*` so the surface stays
self-contained in the single app module (no collisions — verified across Sources + TeslaSync).

